# Experiment data dictionary

All timestamps are UTC RFC 3339 strings unless a field explicitly says
monotonic nanoseconds or elapsed seconds. All digests are lowercase hexadecimal
SHA-256. Empty string in CSV represents JSON `null`; it never means zero or
failure. The independent experimental unit for system-level analysis is one
scheduled episode, not a frame, action, model call, or monitor poll.

This is the post-v7, post-pilot documentation contract. Production v6 is
preserved `INVALID_HARNESS` after its camera source starved and a valid raw tick
collided on the CFR grid; v7 is preserved `INVALID_HARNESS` after an over-rate
raw camera acquisition in a later slot reached the writer. The replacement
continuous-acquisition, same-slot/raw-cadence filter, and source-freshness
implementation passes the 190-test experiment suite but has no
production-pilot result. This contract has not been
snapshotted into a locked campaign, and no locked campaign has been frozen,
approved, or run.

## Campaign-level artifacts

### `CAMPAIGN_MANIFEST.json`

| Field | Type | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `schema_version` | integer | Manifest schema, currently 1 |
| `campaign_id` | string | Versioned, path-safe campaign identity |
| `mode` | `pilot` or `locked` | Scientific data phase |
| `frozen_utc` | timestamp | Time the immutable snapshot was created |
| `protocol_path`, `protocol_sha256` | string, digest | Exact protocol snapshot and content hash |
| `schedule_path`, `schedule_sha256`, `schedule_size` | string, digest, integer | Frozen randomized CSV and entry count |
| `sequential_execution` | Boolean | True: at most one registry attempt may be open |
| `common_random_numbers` | Boolean | True: matched profiles share generated-instance seed/CRN key |
| `reuse_policy` | enum | `fresh_attempts_only`; shared-reference reuse is reserved and refused |
| `max_infrastructure_attempts` | integer | Exactly 3; valid system failures never consume a retry |
| `locked_approval_required` | Boolean | Locked registry refuses `begin` before exact approval |
| `provenance.git_commit` | string or null | Repository commit at freeze |
| `provenance.dirty`, `git_status_sha256`, `dirty_patch_sha256` | Boolean/digests | Dirty-state declaration and hashes without secret key material |
| `provenance.source_roots[]` | paths | Repository-relative roots whose membership is recomputed, including relevant tests |
| `provenance.source_files[]` | objects | Repository-relative path, content digest, and bytes for every relevant source file |
| `provenance.frozen_input_roots[]` | paths | Exact config/protocol roots whose membership is recomputed |
| `provenance.frozen_inputs[]` | objects | Repository-relative path, digest, and bytes for explicit configs/protocol inputs |
| `manifest_sha256` | digest | Canonical JSON hash computed with this field omitted |
| `metadata.analysis_spec` | object | Frozen outcomes/reference, episode/CRN/Holm method, and exact schedule-derived matrix/profile families |
| `metadata.execution_engine` | object | Locked exact engine ID, module, class, repository-relative source, and verified source hash |

`PROTOCOL.md` is the byte-exact protocol snapshot. `PROTOCOL.sha256` contains
one GNU-style line for it. `environment/provenance.json` duplicates the
provenance record for direct inspection. `EXCLUSIONS.md` and `CHANGELOG.md` are
append-only human records; they do not authorize mutation of frozen inputs.

### `run_schedule.csv`

| Column | Type | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `schedule_id` | string | Stable `S000001`-style randomized assignment ID |
| `schedule_position` | integer | One-based sole permitted sequential order |
| `block_id`, `block_position` | string, integer | Matched block and randomized within-block profile position |
| `matrix_id` | string | Main, topology, ablation, sensitivity, or explicit custom matrix |
| `scenario_id`, `scenario_variant_id` | strings | Template and split-specific held-out instance definition |
| `profile_id` | string | Evaluated topology/ablation/baseline profile |
| `model_backbone` | string | Frozen model label resolved to exact ID/hash in setup provenance |
| `repetition` | integer | One-based matched repetition within cell |
| `seed` | non-negative integer | Generated-instance/controller seed shared by the block |
| `split` | string | `pilot`, `locked`, or `locked_test` as validated by campaign mode |
| `executor` | string | `synthetic_event`, `mujoco`, `human_executor`, or `real_robot` |
| `crn_key` | string | Pre-profile matched-instance identity |
| `reuse_group` | null | Reserved; shared-reference outcome reuse is not implemented |

### `RUN_STATE.json` and `run_index.csv`

`RUN_STATE.json` is authoritative; `run_index.csv` is regenerated from it.
Top-level fields include the immutable campaign/protocol/schedule identities,
approval state, retry limit, monotonic `registry_revision`, entries, and an
append-only transition event list.

Each entry stores the exact schedule assignment, latest `status`, all attempts,
optional `disposition`, and a one-use `retry_authorization`. Each attempt stores:

| Field | Type | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `attempt_number`, `attempt_id` | integer, string | Contiguous preserved identity; never reused |
| `status` | status enum | `NOT_RUN` while open, then sealed once |
| `started_utc`, `ended_utc` | timestamps | Reservation and seal times |
| `oracle_verdict` | string or null | Objective oracle result, separate from status/diagnosis |
| `reason` | string or null | Infrastructure, harness, or safety disposition evidence |
| `artifact_path` | relative path | Exact `episodes/<schedule>/attempt_<n>` tree |
| `artifact_audit_passed` | Boolean or null | Result known at registry seal time |
| `infrastructure_evidence` | object or null | Attempt-local external-outage evidence path and SHA-256, required for infrastructure status |
| `recovery_authorization` | object or null | Consumed recovery-report path/hash/time binding for a retry |

Statuses have these non-overlapping meanings:

| Status | Meaning and analysis treatment |
|---|---|
| `VALID_PASS` | Studied system produced a passing outcome and artifact audit passed; no retry |
| `VALID_SYSTEM_FAILURE` | Studied system produced a failing outcome and artifact audit passed; retained as data, no retry |
| `INFRA_INTERRUPTED` | Independently documented external availability interruption; retry blocks until hashed restoration/two-check/smoke evidence is authorized; same seed, maximum three attempts |
| `INVALID_HARNESS` | Recorder/oracle/driver invalidated measurement; preserved, not silently retried in the same campaign |
| `ABORTED_SAFETY` | Safe stop occurred; preserved separately and counted per preregistered outcome/exclusion rule |
| `NOT_RUN` | Randomized assignment has no sealed measurement or its current reservation is open |

An oracle verdict answers whether declared expectations passed. A diagnosis is
a later causal assessment. Neither field is inferred from the other.

## Attempt-level artifacts

| Artifact | Source-of-truth content |
|---|---|
| `setup.json`, `SETUP.md` | Campaign/attempt identity, profile graph, mechanisms, models, hashes, service health, scene, budgets, schedule position, reproduction command |
| `events.jsonl` | Append-only chronological source of truth with stable event IDs, UTC/monotonic/video time, states, requests, actions, decisions, triggers, observations, errors |
| `experiment_record.md` | Generated rendering of `events.jsonl`; never hand-authored evidence |
| `runtime_states.jsonl` | Ordered evaluated-system state snapshots |
| `hidden_states.jsonl` | Scoring-only simulator state; never an evaluated-agent input |
| `oracle_observations.jsonl` | Raw objective observations keyed by oracle ID |
| `frame_requests.jsonl` | Logical request-to-exact-transport-image mapping, optional lossless source-image mapping, and response/event links |
| `frames/` | Content-addressed exact transport image bytes and, for lossy transports, the lossless source capture from which they were deterministically encoded |
| `model_calls.jsonl`, `model_calls/` | Timings/IDs plus redacted application-level semantic request (including bound tool schemas/options), parsed response, malformed semantic response, and error artifacts. SAM additionally retains its exact transport image body/hash; exact raw HTTP request/response bytes for upper model and embedding clients are not captured |
| `inputs.json` | Frozen episode inputs, user script, and generated instance parameters |
| `initial_state.json`, `final_state.json` | Initial and available final hidden scoring state |
| `initial.png`, `final.png` | Corresponding visual state when available |
| `results.json`, `results.md` | Status, separate oracle verdict, outcomes, metrics, and generated rendering |
| `diagnosis.md` | Post-run expected/observed comparison, first divergence, layer, competing causes, confidence, and evidence links |
| `terminal.log` | Redacted timestamped operational output |
| `video.mp4`, `robot_camera.mp4` | Synchronized composite and clean first-person recording |
| `video_metadata.json` | Monotonic origin, UTC mapping, codec/FPS/resolution/frame/duration and coverage checks |
| `artifact_checks.json` | Structural, semantic, timing, frame, call, and video audit result |
| `checksums.sha256` | Sorted digest of every regular attempt artifact except itself |

Every JSONL line is one strict JSON object. Event IDs are contiguous
`E000001`-style strings. `elapsed_seconds` and `video_time_seconds` share one
monotonic origin. Secret values are removed; redaction paths/counts are
evidence, but secret values or reversible derivatives are never retained.

### `frame_requests.jsonl`

Each `frame_request` record maps one logical request to the exact image bytes
used by its transport:

| Field | Type | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `request_id`, `logical_agent` | strings | Stable request identity and receiving logical role/service |
| `capture_utc`, `capture_monotonic_ns`, `capture_elapsed_seconds` | timestamp/integer/number | Capture time on the attempt's shared UTC/monotonic clock |
| `camera_view_id`, `frame_sequence_number`, `camera_frame_id` | strings/integer/string | Exact camera/view and sequence identity linked to video metadata |
| `image_path` | relative path | Content-addressed file containing the exact image byte sequence supplied to the transport; for lossy SAM transport, this is the exact deterministic JPEG actually sent |
| `raw_image_sha256` | digest | SHA-256 of the exact transport file bytes stored at `image_path`, including the exact JPEG bytes for SAM |
| `source_image_path` | relative path or null | Optional content-addressed lossless capture used to derive a lossy transport image; null when `image_path` is already the lossless source |
| `source_raw_image_sha256` | digest or null | SHA-256 of the lossless bytes at `source_image_path`; present and absent together with that path |
| `source_frame_sha256` | digest | SHA-256 of the decoded lossless source pixels, used to bind the capture to the robot-camera video source |
| `encoded_request_payload_sha256` | digest | SHA-256 of the exact supplied image payload representation (raw bytes or encoded data URL/base64 text as applicable) |
| `prompt_request_body_sha256` | digest | SHA-256 of the exact request/body representation associated with this frame |
| `persisted_request_body_sha256` | digest | SHA-256 commitment to the exact redacted request-body representation that the raw model-call artifact must preserve |
| `expected_request_redaction_paths` | list of strings | Exact JSON paths expected to be redacted when persisting the request, independently checked against the redaction journal |
| `response_id`, `event_ids` | string/list | Response and stable event links, either on this record or a later `frame_response_link` record |

For a lossy transport, the two representations have different purposes and
must not be substituted for one another. `image_path`, `raw_image_sha256`, the
redacted raw request, and the model-call artifact retain the exact JPEG sent to
SAM. `source_image_path`, `source_raw_image_sha256`, and
`source_frame_sha256` retain the lossless capture and pixel identity. The video
auditor decodes the lossless source image and compares its pixel digest and
camera-frame ID to `video_metadata.json`; it never compares recompressed JPEG
pixels to a lossless video-source hash.

A visual `model_call_start` binds its logical request through
`frame_request_ids`. The current contract is intentionally singular: a visual
call must name exactly one frame request, and the persisted raw request must
contain exactly one distinct recognized image matching that frame's exact
transport bytes and encoded-payload hash. Nested HRI/Planner calls and
sequential Validator calls may each bind different captures. A single call
containing multiple distinct views is rejected as ambiguous; multi-view
validation must currently accumulate one view per Validator call.

Every frame request has exactly one terminal link:

| Record type | Required fields | Meaning and audit rule |
|---|---|---|
| `frame_response_link` | `request_id`, `response_id`, `event_ids` | Binds the frame to a successful model-call end and matching `model_response` event; the link timestamp cannot predate call completion |
| `frame_error_link` | `request_id`, `call_id`, `event_ids` | Binds a transport/service failure without fabricating a response ID; accepted only when the call start owns that frame request, the call ends as `model_call_error`, a matching `model_error` event has the same request/call IDs, and the link follows call completion |

Both link records also receive the standard JSONL UTC, monotonic, and elapsed
fields. Missing, duplicate, cross-call, prematurely timestamped, or semantically
inconsistent terminal links invalidate the artifact audit.

## Analysis outputs

Binary ITT summaries report assigned, resolved, successes, failures, missing,
missing-by-status, observed rate, Wilson interval, and fixed-denominator
best/worst bounds. `estimable=false`, `estimate=null`, and a non-empty `reason`
are mandatory when assignments remain unresolved.

`analysis_gate` records locked approval, registry completion, unresolved
outcomes, artifact-audit state, and whether live source was checked. Merely
having `mode=locked` does not yield the `confirmatory_locked` label.

Matched comparisons report candidate/complete/incomplete blocks, discordant and
tied pairs, matched risk difference, percentile bootstrap interval, exact
McNemar/binomial p-value, and Holm-adjusted p-value within the frozen family.
Pilot power records planned episode-pair count, empirical power, Monte Carlo
Wilson interval, simulations, alpha, and method. Failure taxonomy counts status,
post-run failure layer, and primary diagnosis separately.

The binary GLMM CLI writes an immutable envelope containing `analysis_kind`,
the input rows/config/source SHA-256 digests, and a `report`. A fit report names
the exact model specification, treatment references, optimizer/software,
convergence and separation diagnostics, random-effect estimates, marginal
contrasts, per-template raw outcomes, and canonical input digest. A power report
records candidate repetitions, alpha, target power, simulation seed/count,
minimum absolute difference, invalid-fit nondetections, power curve, and selected
`r` or an explicit not-estimable reason. The adjacent `.sha256` binds the whole
envelope. No real paired T5/B1 production-pilot GLMM or power envelope exists;
the six clean instrumentation pilots are excluded from this fit and cannot
select `r`.

No `NaN`, infinity, empty-string-as-zero, frame-level pseudo-replication, or
silent complete-case substitution is permitted in publication tables.
